nt_uuid":"6545216d-c4da-4ab1-80e9-aeb36f81ae6a","position":{"commit_sha":"72f4c3bf3c5d54c767359cccc2f3e99922e85b74","position":"1795388820420619001-6545216d-c4da-4ab1-80e9-aeb36f81ae6a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"81ce9e7ee0d235a18f64a060fe9b405fb42ad5ec05498da367f0f73f288ddc09","event_uuid":"c2645c0a-fc1f-4cad-898f-aed446a35d59","position":{"commit_sha":"19a3203380a12c9f0a94b580a5122e55a011b3b0","position":"1795398163344112026-c2645c0a-fc1f-4cad-898f-aed446a35d59"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"755a4c94da6b0d49bddf8b113db97abf7412f521e697b95ddffb5aa5fa2a7d61","event_uuid":"0a9cd564-7980-48b6-997f-ae9ebf02349e","position":{"commit_sha":"48b4fff4be176e315bcb691976ea3e63b72565e4","position":"1795398640030528001-0a9cd564-7980-48b6-997f-ae9ebf02349e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-311_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"05f74084-8156-4489-b43f-fbb9222cdc20","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Cause triage (2026-11-21 PST, run 44681457334 tracebacks read against origin/main 1a11014a3a4); no fix started, ticket left open. Product defects found: (1) src/rebar/_store/git_locking.py:34-37,191 makes the store git advisory lock (bug 9305) a no-op where fcntl is absent, although src/rebar/_store/lock_kernel.py already has the msvcrt leg (take_exclusive/release_exclusive/is_contention); test_git_contention_9305's holder also imports fcntl. (2) src/rebar/_proc.py reap_process_group only proc.kill()s on non-POSIX (killpg is POSIX-only, harness.py:174-175 sets start_new_session only on posix), so on Windows a grounding tool's pipe-holding grandchild survives a timeout; test_harness's reproduction uses os.fork and should use a Popen grandchild. Test-side or POSIX-only: test_compact_trigger_shared_sidecars.py:106 and test_recent_creates_shared_journal.py:151 call select.select on a pipe (WinError 10038), replace with a bounded reader thread; test_gate_admission_09da.py:293 uses signal.SIGKILL, use proc.kill(); doctor_locks' contended-leg test holds with fcntl in its child, use lock_kernel; test_footprint and test_tracker_footprint_cli expect st_blocks allocation, while src/rebar/_store/footprint.py:26,70 deliberately reports unavailable (expect that on Windows); peak RSS is None without resource (src/rebar/llm/peak_rss.py:40), decide: product Windows measure (GetProcessMemoryInfo via ctypes) or expect None; test_opcert_producer_seam (0o600) and test_opcert_own_pub_resolution (read-only dir) and test_ensure_pandoc (exec bit) rely on POSIX mode bits: skip with reason, and file a bug that the op-cert private key gets no ACL restriction on Windows; test_snapshot_janitor open-reader eviction: os.rename of a directory with an open file fails on Windows, so janitor.py:211-214 returns 0 and leaves the entry (needs a decision: Windows eviction cannot be rename-first).","timestamp":1795261639280180001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implemented on worktree b5-aerial-flameproof-antbear, commit ca6d8e8018b (on origin/main 39d78c81fd5). Product: git_locking takes both advisory locks through lock_kernel (msvcrt leg on Windows; with no leg it returns before creating a lock file); _proc.reap_process_group off POSIX also terminates every descendant found by a Toolhelp parent-pid walk (best-effort). Implementation note beyond the plan text: test_acli_subprocess_timeout.py::test_non_posix_reaper_uses_kill_not_killpg forces os.name=nt with a fake pid 4321 and has no POSIX_ONLY marker, so on the Windows sweep the real walk would have terminated any runner process naming 4321 as parent; the test now stubs _windows_process_table to an empty table (file added to file_impact). Removed 9 lines from posix-api.args; 6 remain: test_opcert_own_pub_resolution_d26a::test_certifies_when_the_key_dir_is_read_only (now skipped on Windows: chmod cannot make a Windows directory unwritable - intentionally unsupported), 3 test_gate_peak_rss_9ea3 lines (decision b), test_snapshot_janitor::test_eviction_rename_to_trash_open_reader_survives (decision a), test_opcert_producer_seam_8d8e::test_key_genesis_permissions_and_gitignore (decision c). macOS: 220 targeted tests pass; ruff, complexity ratchet and mechanism ratchet (exit 0) clean. Windows validation dispatched 2026-11-22 13:26 PST: test.yml run 45072089680 on tmp/b5-aerial-flameproof-antbear. make verify running. Decision (c) note: cloistered-decomposed-nymph (closed) already records the operator decision (option 3, 2026-11-18) that Windows relies on the default ACL, with icacls evidence that ssh-keygen gives the minted key owner/SYSTEM/Administrators only.","timestamp":1795382801411896001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pre-merge Windows validation: test.yml run 45072089680, sweep (windows) job 137361100569 on tmp/b5-aerial-flameproof-antbear at ca6d8e8018b (posix-api.args reduced to the 6 remaining lines): 20730 passed, 892 skipped, 0 failed, 0 errors (finished 2026-11-22 14:50 PST). The 9 removed tests are all collected under the sweep's -m 'not integration and not external' selection (pytest --collect-only on ca6d8e8018b lists all 9); none carries a skip marker that fires on Windows (doctor_locks' requires_posix_named_semaphore probe passed on Windows in run 44681457334, where that test ran and failed); so each passed. tests/unit/test_proc_reap_windows.py ran there too. make verify on ca6d8e8018b: default tier 5 failed / 21758 passed in 1:29:56 under host load avg ~24 (a colima VM from other sessions at ~570% CPU); all 5 were timeouts (4 pytest-timeout 300 s, 1 observability.sh 135 s subprocess timeout) in modules this change does not touch, and all 14 tests of those selections pass in isolation on the same tree. Re-running make verify before any push.","timestamp":1795388820420619001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"make verify on ca6d8e8018b (attempt 2, 2026-11-22 16:2x-17:1x PST) exited 0: default tier 21763 passed / 34 skipped, integration 231 passed / 2 skipped (log /Users/joeoakhart/rebar/.rebar/scratch/05f74084-jerboa/make-verify-antbear2.log). Landed: Gerrit 3528 patch set 1 (ca6d8e8018bee2e3950e184b31487ba880330bbd) at LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, 0 unresolved; submitted revision-scoped; merged to main as 13d4a73cde21c3efc2ce3b927950eeb806ec82d3. Ticket stays in_progress. Remaining work: (1) AC1 evidence from the first scheduled main test.yml run containing 13d4a73cde2; (2) AC2: 5 of the 6 remaining posix-api.args lines wait on design decisions held by the coordinator - (a) janitor rename-first eviction with an open reader (test_snapshot_janitor::test_eviction_rename_to_trash_open_reader_survives), (b) peak RSS on Windows (3 test_gate_peak_rss_9ea3 lines), (c) op-cert key mode on Windows (test_opcert_producer_seam_8d8e::test_key_genesis_permissions_and_gitignore; cloistered-decomposed-nymph already holds an operator decision that Windows relies on the default ACL, so applying the same skip-with-reason is the likely path, pending confirmation). The 6th line, test_opcert_own_pub_resolution_d26a::test_certifies_when_the_key_dir_is_read_only, is intentionally unsupported on Windows: chmod cannot make a Windows directory unwritable (the read-only attribute is ignored on directories), and the test now skips there with that reason.","timestamp":1795398640030528001}],"created_at":1795153838950093001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"d6e40f62-2b90-4deb-8f6d-8d2246ad74ea","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"8aa0-2120-5ef3-4750"},{"link_uuid":"c2645c0a-fc1f-4cad-898f-aed446a35d59","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"4822-eaee-518d-4746"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nDiscovered while triaging breezy-hogged-mastiff, which owns `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/unclassified.args`. These 15 entries move to `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/posix-api.args`, which this bug owns.\n\nSignatures read in run 44681457334: `os.fork` absent (`tests/unit/grounding/test_harness.py`), `signal.SIGKILL` absent (`test_gate_admission_09da.py`), `select` on a pipe raises `WinError 10038` (`test_compact_trigger_shared_sidecars.py`, `test_recent_creates_shared_journal.py`), `os.stat_result.st_blocks` absent (`tests/unit/store/test_footprint.py`, `tests/interfaces/test_tracker_footprint_cli.py` reports allocation `unavailable`), peak RSS is None without `resource` (`test_gate_peak_rss_9ea3.py`), POSIX mode bits not honoured (`test_opcert_producer_seam_8d8e.py` 0o666 vs 0o600, `tests/scripts/test_ensure_pandoc.py` exec bit, `test_opcert_own_pub_resolution_d26a.py` read-only dir still writable), a subprocess lock holder that never takes its `fcntl` lock (`test_doctor_locks.py::test_a_contended_fcntl_leg_reads_as_held`, `test_git_contention_9305.py`), and an evicted snapshot directory still present while a reader holds it open (`test_snapshot_janitor.py`).\n\nEvidence: Windows runs on throwaway branch `tmp/w05-remeasure` (origin/main `717c50f8b33` plus a selection-only workflow change): run 44665461131 and run 44681457334 (JUnit XML with full tracebacks), both 2026-11-19 PST. Per-test causes: ticket comment of 2026-11-21.\n\n## Root cause\nProduct:\n1. `src/rebar/_store/git_locking.py` imports `fcntl` itself (:34-37) and returns unlocked when it is absent (`_store_git_op_lock` :191, `fetch_coordination_lock`, `_acquire_fetch_coord_flock`). On Windows the per-store git-op lock (bug 9305) and the common-dir fetch lock are no-ops, although `src/rebar/_store/lock_kernel.py` has an `msvcrt` leg used by every other store lock.\n2. `src/rebar/_proc.py` `reap_process_group` only calls `proc.kill()` off POSIX (`killpg` is POSIX-only), so a timed-out child's pipe-holding grandchild survives on Windows.\nTest-side: `select.select` on a pipe, `signal.SIGKILL`, `os.fork`, `fcntl` in a child lock holder, `st_blocks` and exec-bit assertions with no Windows branch.\n\n## Approach (this change)\n- `git_locking`: take and release both locks through `lock_kernel.take_exclusive` / `release_exclusive`; a platform with neither leg (`NoExclusiveLegError`) still proceeds unlocked. Same bounded wait, same \"advisory, proceed on exhaustion\" contract. Drop the module's own `fcntl` import; `tests/unit/store/test_git_locking_no_fcntl.py` patches `lock_kernel.fcntl`/`msvcrt` instead.\n- `_proc.reap_process_group` off POSIX keeps `proc.kill()` then `proc.wait(timeout=grace + drain)`, and between them terminates every descendant of the child: a `CreateToolhelp32Snapshot` walk (ctypes, Windows only) collects processes whose parent-pid chain leads to `proc.pid`, and each gets `TerminateProcess`; a second pass catches any started meanwhile. Windows never re-parents, and the un-waited Popen handle keeps the child's pid from being reused, so the walk also finds a grandchild whose parent already exited (the case `taskkill /T` cannot reach). The walk is best-effort: any failure (no `kernel32` on a forced-`nt` POSIX test host, access denied) is logged at debug and the reap proceeds as before. POSIX path unchanged. No config key, env var or flag. The 2 forced-`nt` tests in `tests/unit/reconciler/state/test_acli_subprocess_timeout.py` (`_FakeProc` with `pid`/`kill`/`wait`) keep passing unchanged because kill+wait stay and the walk failure is caught.\n- Tests: `test_harness` grandchild via `subprocess.Popen` writing its pid, polled (bounded, 10 s) until dead after the timeout on every platform, since on POSIX a killed orphan stays a zombie until init reaps it (liveness via `lock_owner._pid_alive`, never `os.kill(pid, 0)`, which terminates on Windows); new `tests/unit/test_proc_reap_windows.py` pins the descendant walk (pure parent-pid closure, deepest-first order, an exited parent's orphan included) and the best-effort fallback with a fake snapshot/terminate pair on every platform. `test_compact_trigger_shared_sidecars` / `test_recent_creates_shared_journal` read the holder's line through a bounded reader thread. `test_gate_admission_09da` uses `holder.kill()`. `test_doctor_locks` and `test_git_contention_9305` holders lock through `lock_kernel`. `test_footprint` / `test_tracker_footprint_cli` expect the documented `unavailable` allocation where `os.stat_result` has no `st_blocks` (`footprint.py:26,70`). `test_ensure_pandoc` checks the exec bit only where POSIX mode bits exist.\n- `test_opcert_own_pub_resolution_d26a::test_certifies_when_the_key_dir_is_read_only` skips on Windows (\"chmod cannot make a Windows directory unwritable\"); its line stays and is recorded here as intentionally unsupported.\n- Remove the 9 fixed lines from `posix-api.args`.\n\n## Not in this change (design decisions pending with the coordinator)\n(a) janitor rename-first eviction with an open reader (`test_snapshot_janitor.py`, `janitor.py:211-214`); (b) peak RSS on Windows (3 `test_gate_peak_rss_9ea3.py` lines, `peak_rss.py:40`); (c) op-cert key ACL on Windows (`test_opcert_producer_seam_8d8e.py`). Their 5 lines stay. This ticket stays in_progress until they are decided and done; it is not closed on this change.\n\n## Scope\nsrc/rebar/_store/git_locking.py, src/rebar/_store/lock_kernel.py (docstring caller list), src/rebar/_proc.py, tests/unit/test_proc_reap_windows.py (new), tests/unit/reconciler/state/test_acli_subprocess_timeout.py (must pass unchanged), the 10 test modules named above, tests/unit/store/test_git_locking_no_fcntl.py, .github/windows-sweep-deselect/posix-api.args.\n\n## Testing\nPre-merge: push the tree to `tmp/b5-aerial-flameproof-antbear`, dispatch `test.yml`, record the `sweep (windows)` run id, show each removed test was collected, carries no skip marker that fires on Windows (read from the diff) and is absent from the failure and error list of a job with 0 failed and 0 errors; delete the branch. Post-merge: first scheduled main `test.yml` run containing the merge (AC1). `make verify` before push.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every line removed from `posix-api.args` names a test that passed in a `sweep (windows)` run on main after the fix (run id recorded in a comment).\n- [ ] `posix-api.args` is empty and deleted with its reference in `.github/workflows/test.yml`, or each remaining line names a test recorded on this ticket as intentionally unsupported on Windows with the reason.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_store/git_locking.py","reason":"aerial-flameproof-antbear: store git-op and fetch locks through lock_kernel (msvcrt leg on Windows)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/lock_kernel.py","reason":"aerial-flameproof-antbear: docstring: list the git_locking callers"},{"path":"src/rebar/_proc.py","reason":"aerial-flameproof-antbear: reap_process_group kills the process tree on Windows"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_proc_reap_windows.py","reason":"aerial-flameproof-antbear: pins taskkill argv and fallback"},{"path":"tests/unit/store/test_git_locking_no_fcntl.py","reason":"aerial-flameproof-antbear: patch lock_kernel instead of git_locking.fcntl"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_git_contention_9305.py","reason":"aerial-flameproof-antbear: holder locks through lock_kernel"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/test_tracker_footprint_cli.py","reason":"aerial-flameproof-antbear: expect unavailable allocation without st_blocks"},{"path":"tests/scripts/graph/test_doctor_locks.py","reason":"aerial-flameproof-antbear: holder locks through lock_kernel"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_ensure_pandoc.py","reason":"aerial-flameproof-antbear: exec bit only where POSIX mode bits exist"},{"path":"tests/unit/grounding/test_harness.py","reason":"aerial-flameproof-antbear: Popen grandchild, asserted dead"},{"path":"tests/unit/store/test_footprint.py","reason":"aerial-flameproof-antbear: expect unavailable allocation without st_blocks"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_compact_trigger_shared_sidecars.py","reason":"aerial-flameproof-antbear: bounded reader thread instead of select"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_recent_creates_shared_journal.py","reason":"aerial-flameproof-antbear: bounded reader thread instead of select"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gate_admission_09da.py","reason":"aerial-flameproof-antbear: holder.kill instead of SIGKILL"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_opcert_own_pub_resolution_d26a.py","reason":"aerial-flameproof-antbear: skip read-only-dir test on Windows"},{"path":".github/windows-sweep-deselect/posix-api.args","reason":"aerial-flameproof-antbear: remove each fixed line"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/state/test_acli_subprocess_timeout.py","reason":"aerial-flameproof-antbear: forced-nt fake-pid test must not walk real Windows processes"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","4822-eaee-518d-4746"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"a1b999a4-5b12-4195-9cfd-58a81415cdb1","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["windows","portability"],"ticket_id":"8896-1f18-0965-4f1f","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Windows sweep: 15 tests use POSIX-only process, file-system and permission APIs","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["004e0099-7378-4de5-8101-73931b8f3983","f243bbc3-417c-4df8-9123-f8af9e56744b","bf03e39e-a88c-4787-9646-3e4a14d55894","3dec53ed-00b7-4275-bb5c-2979f1cf9b69","6960a973-8324-4af4-9123-cecc78bff9d9","a1b999a4-5b12-4195-9cfd-58a81415cdb1","8a548fda-7d55-4a75-9f9f-bbe4366b0fdb","8fb15a62-c6e9-4391-9e91-031c5ca8e921","c5db9372-195d-430a-93ff-79d0cfa03f3e","6545216d-c4da-4ab1-80e9-aeb36f81ae6a","c2645c0a-fc1f-4cad-898f-aed446a35d59","0a9cd564-7980-48b6-997f-ae9ebf02349e"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795398640030528002,"uuid":"8bfa0068-f160-4ac2-aef1-105b91adc336"}